TEXT 160 0 Left 3 ;#31 Phase splitter, the circuit behind the ADD and INVERT demonstration
TEXT 160 64 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zsy-pxpfB4o
TEXT 160 112 Left 2 ;Equal collector and emitter resistors give two outputs of the same size and opposite
TEXT 160 144 Left 2 ;phase, so adding them cancels the signal and subtracting them doubles it.
TEXT 1180 256 Left 2 !.tran 0 50m 45m 1u
TEXT 1180 296 Left 2 !.meas tran VC_AVG AVG V(collector)
TEXT 1180 336 Left 2 !.meas tran VE_AVG AVG V(emitter)
TEXT 1180 376 Left 2 !.meas tran VC_PP PP V(collector)
TEXT 1180 416 Left 2 !.meas tran VE_PP PP V(emitter)
TEXT 1180 456 Left 2 !.meas tran SUM_PP PP V(collector)+V(emitter)
TEXT 1180 496 Left 2 !.meas tran DIFF_PP PP V(collector)-V(emitter)
TEXT 160 760 Left 2 ;Alan's drawing gives +5 V, 20K, 10K and 2.2K in both the collector and the emitter, and shows the
TEXT 160 792 Left 2 ;generator coupled in through a capacitor without naming its value. The 1 uF, the 0.5 V amplitude
TEXT 160 824 Left 2 ;and the 1 kHz are chosen here; 0.5 V keeps the collector clear of the 5 V rail.
